214:/// when set (non-empty); otherwise the twin is base64-decoded. Returns
215:/// null when neither is set. Both set: the twin must decode to exactly
216:/// the plain value — same value is fine, anything else is ambiguous and
217:/// fails loud instead of picking one silently. Malformed base64 fails
